desktop-shell: folders in the Start menu

A [launcher] with "folder=NAME" is not listed in the main Start menu but
inside a folder: the main list shows one row for the folder (folder icon,
name and an arrow) where its first launcher would be; clicking it shows
the folder's launchers, with a "< NAME" row at the top to go back. The menu
keeps one size, enough for the main list and for every folder.

hexaOS uses it for the Flatpak apps (folder=Apps in ~/.config/hexaos/apps.ini,
written by the hexaOS Store and apps/hexa-launcher).

